==Latin==

===Etymology 1===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*deyḱ-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*deikō}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*déyḱti||to show, point out}} (reformed as a thematic verb). The perfect forms are derived from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*dḗyḱst}}.

Cognates include {{cog|osc|𐌃𐌄𐌝𐌊𐌖𐌌||to show, point out}}, {{cog|sa|दिशति|tr=diśáti}}, {{cog|grc|δείκνυμι}} and {{cog|ang|tǣċan}} (English {{m|ang|teach}}).

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|la|deicō}} {{qual|archaic}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|dīcō}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|irreg|dīcō}}

# to [[say]], [[talk]], [[speak]], [[utter]], [[mention]],
#: {{syn|la|aiō|for|effor|inquam|ōrō|alloquor|loquor}}
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|4|204|thru=205|quote='''dīcitur''' ante ārās media inter nūmina dīvum<br/>multa Iovem manibus supplex ōrāsse supīnīs|trans='''It is said''' [that King Iarbas] – before the altars, amid divine presences all around – often prostrated himself, with hands raised in supplication, to implore Jupiter.}}
#* {{Q|la|Jerome|Vulgate|Genesis|1|3|quote='''dixit'''que Deus fiat lux et facta est lux|trans=And God '''said''': Be light made. And light was made.}}
#: {{uxi|la|Salūtem '''dīcit'''.|lit=He '''says''' health.|He '''says''' hi.}}
# to [[declare]], [[state]]
## to [[affirm]], [[assert]] (positively)
##: {{syn|la|aiō|fīgō|contendō}}
# to [[tell]]
#* {{Q|la|Plautus|Captivi|623|notes=[https://web.archive.org/web/20130113120403/http://www.ihaystack.com/authors/m/plautus_titus_maccius/00016564_amphitryo_asinaria_aulularia_bacchides_captivi_amphi/00016564_englishlatin_utf8_p043.htm English and Latin text]
|quote=Eho '''dic''' mihi, quis illic igitur est?
|t=Hey? '''Tell''' me, who is he then?}}
# to [[appoint]], [[name]], [[nominate]] (to an office)
# to [[call]], name
#* {{Q|la|Ov.|M.|1|5–7|quote=Ante mare et terrās et quod tegit omnia caelum<br>ūnus erat tōtō nātūrae vultus in orbe,<br>quem '''dīxēre''' chaos: {{...}}
|t=Before the sea and the lands and the sky that covers over all things,<br>there was one face of nature in the whole world,<br>which '''they called''' chaos: {{...}}}}
# {{lb|la|law|followed by {{m|la|ad}}}} to [[plead]] (before)
# to [[mean]], speak in [[reference]] to, [[refer]] to

